    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When the medical entrance exam was held on May 3, a courageous whistleblower from Sikar sent the National Testing Agency an email containing leaked PDFs that matched 100% of the chemistry questions. This decisive evidence forced the national testing body to act, leading to a referral to India's federal investigative agency. A crackdown that netted the conspirators followed, with multiple arrests were made, including a hypocrite who betrayed his public stance. Consequently, the tainted examination was annulled, and a justice-restoring re-examination was scheduled for June 21 to ensure fairness for all students.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Hero",
        "fragments": [
          "how-1",
          "why-0",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "how-4"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.95
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The agency that acted on the tip received critical intelligence that triggered the investigation into the compromised insiders who set the exam papers. Following this referral to a federal agency, the investigators who closed in brought the suspects to justice. The perpetrators were apprehended, reinforcing the law enforcement action against the fraud. As a consequence, the exam was cancelled to preserve integrity, and a fair re-test for affected students was arranged for June 21, restoring order to the process.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Hero",
